I am back in the flat.
I put on my pyjamas.
I cough loudly.
My throat hurts a lot.
Suddenly, someone knocks on the door.
I open the door slowly.
Sabine is standing there.
She has a thermos in her hand.
"Hello Maya," Sabine says.
"I hear you through the wall, because you are coughing so much."
"Here is fresh ginger tea for you."
She gives me the thermos.
"Thank you, Sabine," I say.
"My head also hurts."
"You should drink the tea now and just sleep," she says.
She goes back to her flat.
I drink a cup of tea and go to bed.
